{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks","id":991151,"title":"Introductions for new folks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T15:38:38-07:00","id":991151,"title":"Introductions for new folks","content":"So quite a few people in the Kickstarter comments section were sad that the crowdfunding campaign is soon coming to an end and thus the little community built up there will go away. I figured I might as well make things easy and offer everybody new to the forums a place to introduce themselves if they decide to hop on over and join the forums here!<br /> <br /> So by all means, tell us a little about yourself and maybe who your favorite Pantheon is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:23:27-07:00","id":991348,"title":"","content":"Hi everybody! I'm Alex <br /> <br /> I'm new and i'm introducing myself here.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> My full name is Alessandro Mattia Chiappetta (chiappetta spelled like Kiappetta) and i'm from Italy. I'm 23 and... well... i don't know what to say.<br /> <br /> I'm not so good with writing in english, be good with me ok? But i'm learning.<br /> <br /> &quot;Elanconnor&quot; is the name of my first scion in an official and long play, A Manitou/anasazi son of Sedna<br /> <br /> My favourite pantheon is the manitou, i like the shaman things and th connection with nature.<br /> <br /> I pledge 20$ for the 2 pdf books and i'm SO exited about all the second edition.<br /> <br /> Scion is my favourite game so far and i'm a pulp narrator, i love big scene, screams,laughs and exagerated stuff, if my players decide to face a huge troll, a king of the mountain trollhunter style, i'm happy. (This says a lot about me, i guess...)<br /> <br /> <br /> And... i don't know what to say, but i'll answer some questions if somebody has","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:36:26-07:00","id":991368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991348#post991348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everybody! I'm Alex <br /> <br /> I'm new and i'm introducing myself here.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> My full name is Alessandro Mattia Chiappetta (chiappetta spelled like Kiappetta) and i'm from Italy. I'm 23 and... well... i don't know what to say.<br /> <br /> I'm not so good with writing in english, be good with me ok? But i'm learning.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Elanconnor&amp;quot; is the name of my first scion in an official and long play, A Manitou/anasazi son of Sedna<br /> <br /> My favourite pantheon is the manitou, i like the shaman things and th connection with nature.<br /> <br /> I pledge 20$ for the 2 pdf books and i'm SO exited about all the second edition.<br /> <br /> Scion is my favourite game so far and i'm a pulp narrator, i love big scene, screams,laughs and exagerated stuff, if my players decide to face a huge troll, a king of the mountain trollhunter style, i'm happy. (This says a lot about me, i guess...)<br /> <br /> <br /> And... i don't know what to say, but i'll answer some questions if somebody has</div> </div> </div> </div> Hi Alex. Don't worry about your english, its my first language and I still misspell stuff all the time.<br /> <br /> I went with the $20 PDF deal too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:02:01-07:00","id":991376,"title":"","content":"I've been lurking on these forums for a while making the occasional post, but I don't think I've properly introduced myself.<br /> <br /> My name is Michal. I'm transgender, female pronouns please, and a practicing pagan follower of the Norse and Irish gods. More specifically, I follow Thor and Freyja on the Norse side and Brigid on the Irish side.<br /> <br /> Mythology has always been a passion of mine, and my love of it eventually led to me embracing my heritage and reclaiming the gods of my ancestors as my gods.<br /> <br /> Scion means a lot to me because it breathes life back into the myths of old, keeps the memories of the old gods alive and vibrant. It was actually the first edition companion book that taught me about the Tuatha de Dannan and through my own research led to me following Brigid.<br /> <br /> My roommate and I went half and half on the $100 tier on his kickstarter because we know our group will use the physical books, but I also personally backed it at $10 so I could get my name in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:04:33-07:00","id":991379,"title":"","content":"Welcome to all our newcomers! I'm so glad to see this forum finally coming back to life! It's been so quite and boring around here for far too long! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T08:12:08-07:00","id":991399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991376#post991376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been lurking on these forums for a while making the occasional post, but I don't think I've properly introduced myself.<br /> <br /> My name is Michal. I'm transgender, female pronouns please, and a practicing pagan follower of the Norse and Irish gods. More specifically, I follow Thor and Freyja on the Norse side and Brigid on the Irish side.<br /> <br /> Mythology has always been a passion of mine, and my love of it eventually led to me embracing my heritage and reclaiming the gods of my ancestors as my gods.<br /> <br /> Scion means a lot to me because it breathes life back into the myths of old, keeps the memories of the old gods alive and vibrant. It was actually the first edition companion book that taught me about the Tuatha de Dannan and through my own research led to me following Brigid.<br /> <br /> My roommate and I went half and half on the $100 tier on his kickstarter because we know our group will use the physical books, but I also personally backed it at $10 so I could get my name in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hello Michal, welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T08:56:47-07:00","id":991410,"title":"","content":"Hi, my name is Jean-Philippe Lacroix, i'm from Qu\u00e9bec (Canada) and i'm currently writing a thesis in history at a university in montreal.<br /> <br /> Me and my girlfriend are expecting a scion of our own due in may. Which make me think that i'll have to figure out how to build or procure myself a relic.<br /> <br /> I've started writing on these forum a small while back in order to fight against a weird case of social anxiety. I don't have problem talking to people but writing emails, talking on the phone and writing post in a forum absolutely terrifies me. <br /> So far this forum has helped me alot. I no longer seem to have anxiety attacks when i'm about to post something and i've even managed to start threads of my own.<br /> <br /> Scion is probably my absolute favorite game and i pledged 100$ for it. I'm also currently running a vampire the requiem game set in miami in the 80s.<br /> As for my favorite pantheon, i like the aztec a lot but i'm very excited to read the manitou pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T09:08:38-07:00","id":991411,"title":"","content":"I only started posting here during the Kickstarter, so I'll go ahead and say hello even though I've never really been much of a fan of kickstarter comments,--<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hello, there, I'm Brandon!<br /> <br /> I've been playing roleplaying games for the past 20-years, and I first heard about Scion from my interest in Exalted, but I didn't actually get into the game until I found myself on RPGnet watching a bit of a flamewar between people who were arguing about Nobilis/Scion and which game was better at Mythology. It was pretty bitter and messed up, but it captured my attention, and the end result was that I grabbed Scion: Hero and ended up getting all three hardback books and the Companion.<br /> <br /> I even ran a short little one-shot game with a friend of mine, but I was never really able to get very far into 1e Scion due to the rules-system, so when a 2nd edition was announced... color me interested in seeing what came of it. Based on the previews that we've gotten so far, I feel very happy with my decision to throw $85 at getting a hardcopy of the two corebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T09:13:51-07:00","id":991413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991410#post991410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, my name is Jean-Philippe Lacroix, i'm from Qu\u00e9bec (Canada) and i'm currently writing a thesis in history at a university in montreal.<br /> <br /> Me and my girlfriend are expecting a scion of our own due in may. Which make me think that i'll have to figure out how to build or procure myself a relic.<br /> <br /> I've started writing on these forum a small while back in order to fight against a weird case of social anxiety. I don't have problem talking to people but writing emails, talking on the phone and writing post in a forum absolutely terrifies me. <br /> So far this forum has helped me alot. I no longer seem to have anxiety attacks when i'm about to post something and i've even managed to start threads of my own.<br /> <br /> Scion is probably my absolute favorite game and i pledged 100$ for it. I'm also currently running a vampire the requiem game set in miami in the 80s.<br /> As for my favorite pantheon, i like the aztec a lot but i'm very excited to read the manitou pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jean-Phillipr, welcome! I have a similar case of anxiety; talking to people offline is effortless for me, but put me in an online instant messenger and I'm overwhelmed with panic. Here's hoping we can both get better!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:41:25-07:00","id":991440,"title":"","content":"Hey all,<br /> My name is Jim Groves. I usually post under my real name, because it keeps me honest and accountable, but I had an existing forum account so I'm just using it for now.<br /> <br /> I am here at the invitation of the Fabulous Lex!<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been RPing since about 1979 with just about every system under the sun. I'm a freelancer for another game system (Pathfinder), but I always feel cheesy about &quot;flashing credentials&quot; when I am here to post as a fan, like everybody else. I would love to talk to OP about working with them, and there is a set process to do just that, but I just haven't done it yet. <br /> <br /> I loved the original Scion but I set aside when I didn't have the time to debug some of the mechanics. Having looked over the preview materials, I'm really excited about the direction that Neall and the writers have gone in making this new scalable system.<br /> <br /> Glad to meet everybody!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T11:24:47-07:00","id":991458,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm not &quot;new&quot;, as I have lurked among the Scion Community for a while now...<br /> <br /> I'm no stranger to Scion, been with it since it launched. I'm 25 and have been roleplaying since high school. I was first brought into White Wolf (and then into Onyx Path) through Exalted.<br /> <br /> My all-time favorite pantheon is the Tuatha de Dannan, which I had no idea existed before the original Scion Companion. It actually pushed me to study Irish mythology. </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Manann\u00e1n mac Lir is my favorite god among them!<br /> <br /> I pledged at the $100 level and shelled out more money for the dice.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T11:52:19-07:00","id":991466,"title":"","content":"Heyyo new folks!<br /> <br /> I'm not a newbie, but might as well do general introductions. Besides, I didn't post here regularly until the Kickstarter got closer. (Truth be told, it wasn't exactly a HOPPING forum before that)<br /> <br /> Name's Kyman201, but I respond to Ky. I sell bees out in Washington State (Yes, really), and I got into Scion YEARS ago. I even ran two full sagas (Hero to God) using 1E.<br /> <br /> [Traumatic Flashback Joke]<br /> <br /> Dunno if I could pick just one favorite pantheon. I'm looking forward to cutting my teeth on ALL of them come the 2e release.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh right, I backed the 20 dollar tier. I hardly game in person anymore, so I make due with the PDFs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-22-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:07:51-07:00","id":991474,"title":"","content":"I figure I should probably introduce myself: I'm Lex, and while I'm just now coming to Scion with this new edition I've been into tabletop roleplaying for about a decade now, most of that in the World/Chronicles of Darkness gamelines. I'm also a huge history and mythology nerd with a vested interest in the Netjer, as I'm sure the writers are already sick of hearing about.<br /> <br /> It's nice to meet everyone, and I really hope this subforum can get more lively the closer we get to release!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:22:29-07:00","id":991478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991474#post991474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure I should probably introduce myself: I'm Lex, and while I'm just now coming to Scion with this new edition I've been into tabletop roleplaying for about a decade now, most of that in the World/Chronicles of Darkness gamelines. I'm also a huge history and mythology nerd with a vested interest in the Netjer, as I'm sure the writers are already sick of hearing about.<br /> <br /> It's nice to meet everyone, and I really hope this subforum can get more lively the closer we get to release!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from a few details, the above describes me, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My name is Jonathan, though I'll answer to almost anything. This is my first real delve into <i>Scion</i> (I read <i>Hero</i> but never actually played a game with it) and I've been roleplaying for the better part of 20 years: <i>AD&amp;D 2nd Edition</i>, <i>Alternity</i>, <i>New World</i>/<i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> about 6-7 years back, and <i>D&amp;D 5e</i> about 2 years ago when it launched (I didn't do anything with the playtest, though).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:26:54-07:00","id":991481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991413#post991413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jean-Phillipr, welcome! I have a similar case of anxiety; talking to people offline is effortless for me, but put me in an online instant messenger and I'm overwhelmed with panic. Here's hoping we can both get better!</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta say, having attended the Q&amp;A session with you, I find that a bit surprising. :P<br /> <br /> Seriously though, sounds like you're improving on your anxiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:35:54-07:00","id":991486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991474#post991474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nice to meet everyone, and I really hope this subforum can get more lively the closer we get to release!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for starting it and encouraging folks to drop by.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:36:39-07:00","id":991487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991481#post991481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotta say, having attended the Q&amp;A session with you, I find that a bit surprising. :P<br /> <br /> Seriously though, sounds like you're improving on your anxiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bombing poor Neall with HEY PAY ATTENTION TO ME ANSWER MY INANE QUESTION and keeping up a running chat aren't /exactly/ the same thing :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:56:13-07:00","id":991538,"title":"","content":"Maurice here.<br /> <br /> Loved the original game and the concept of it. Backed at the $85 plus dice. <br /> <br /> Hard to say what pantheon is my favorite as they all have aspects I enjoy. Though I'd probably go Egyptian, can't remember proper spelling defaulted, because Anubis is one of my all time favorite gods. <br /> <br /> Like a few backing the game I did get to go to the Q&amp;A at GenCon and honestly was the driving reason I went to GenCon. Though I could have spent the day talking to the panel! Sooooo many questions! <br /> <br /> I to have some social anxiety issues, I brought a folio of character sheets I made to show the panel but in the end I totally chickened out. Did not even get Rich to sign a rack or black vice. Ha ha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:08:23-07:00","id":991546,"title":"","content":"I'm danelsan just about everywhere in the net (I think to this day I have found a single site on which the name was already taken, and that might have been me on a forgotten earlier account). I'm 32 and have been playing RPGs since I was...about 8 or so, in a multitude of different systems.<br /> <br /> I have been on this forum (and predecessors to it) since...about halfway through the Exalted 2e line, I think. I mostly stayed on the Exalted subforum, with sporadic forays into the off-topic one, and even rarer still in others, mostly as a lurker.<br /> <br /> Did not get to play all that much Scion 1e, mostly due to games falling apart because of mechanics flaws we had no time to rewrite or otherwise fix at the time, but I really love the concept of the game, so I was thrilled when 2e was announced, and I liked what I have seen of the system so far.<br /> <br /> Greek and Norse mythology were the most interesting to me for a long time, and I still like them a lot, but I have expanded my horizons a bit over the years (and Scion has been part of that). I'm my group's damn-nearly-always ST, so I'll get to roleplay a variety of deities and scions from all the pantheons anyway ^_^<br /> <br /> I wish I could have put hundreds of dollars on the Scion KS like I did for Exalted 3e, but my family's current financial situation means I have to be a lot more austere with my spending, so I had to go for the $20 for the PDFs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:10:00-07:00","id":991548,"title":"","content":"Hello and Welcome all the new people I hadn't had a chance to greet yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:10:57-07:00","id":991550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991546#post991546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm danelsan just about everywhere in the net (I think to this day I have found a single site on which the name was already taken, and that might have been me on a forgotten earlier account). I'm 32 and have been playing RPGs since I was...about 8 or so, in a multitude of different systems.<br /> <br /> I have been on this forum (and predecessors to it) since...about halfway through the Exalted 2e line, I think. I mostly stayed on the Exalted subforum, with sporadic forays into the off-topic one, and even rarer still in others, mostly as a lurker.<br /> <br /> Did not get to play all that much Scion 1e, mostly due to games falling apart because of mechanics flaws we had no time to rewrite or otherwise fix at the time, but I really love the concept of the game, so I was thrilled when 2e was announced, and I liked what I have seen of the system so far.<br /> <br /> Greek and Norse mythology were the most interesting to me for a long time, and I still like them a lot, but I have expanded my horizons a bit over the years (and Scion has been part of that). I'm my group's damn-nearly-always ST, so I'll get to roleplay a variety of deities and scions from all the pantheons anyway ^_^<br /> <br /> I wish I could have put hundreds of dollars on the Scion KS like I did for Exalted 3e, but my family's current financial situation means I have to be a lot more austere with my spending, so I had to go for the $20 for the PDFs</div> </div> </div> </div> Hopefully things improve for you, good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:23:35-07:00","id":991584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991487#post991487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bombing poor Neall with HEY PAY ATTENTION TO ME ANSWER MY INANE QUESTION and keeping up a running chat aren't /exactly/ the same thing :P</div> </div> </div> </div>An hour for the Q&amp;A was not enough time! I'm glad for all the questions everyone else asked but at the same time I was totally thinking to myself &quot;can you all be quite I just have a few more thousand quick in depth esay style questions to ask before he hour is up!!&quot; <br /> <br /> I mean that in a good way. Like a kid at Christmas bouncing in the chair happy to see what a friend got for a gift but I know there are more for me as well. Ever asked great questions! <br /> <br /> I was the big bearded guy that asked about Aberrant and also the options in the new Scion for non human looking characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:12:27-07:00","id":991714,"title":"","content":"I'm Nyx, though in the spirit of sharing, y'all can call me Viv. I'm transwoman from frosty Michigan, in the US. I'm 27, and I've been playing tabletop games since about 2004. I am an English and Women and Gender Studies dual major.<br /> <br /> I'm also a pagan, a follower of the Asatru. Needless to say, I'm psyched for the Norse write up. Second place goes to the Manitou. I only had the cash for the two pdf $20 deal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:47:11-07:00","id":991734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991714#post991714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Nyx, though in the spirit of sharing, y'all can call me Viv. I'm transwoman from frosty Michigan, in the US. I'm 27, and I've been playing tabletop games since about 2004. I am an English and Women and Gender Studies dual major.<br /> <br /> I'm also a pagan, a follower of the Asatru. Needless to say, I'm psyched for the Norse write up. Second place goes to the Manitou. I only had the cash for the two pdf $20 deal</div> </div> </div> </div>Lot of us out here!<br /> <br /> I'm a staunch atheist, but I'm a anthropologist with a lifelong love of myth, so I'm in for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T00:50:49-07:00","id":991767,"title":"","content":"Howdy new people!<br /> <br /> I'm Andrew McGraw, username Prometheus878, 28 year old white male from Georgia, USA. Big fan of Scion, also big into Exalted and a fan of Trinity.<br /> <br /> To sum up my life story, I was an awkward child, then an awkward teenager, and now I'm a slightly less awkward adult. Yup, that just about covers it.<br /> <br /> Current favorite pantheon is the one I'm most familiar with, the Theoi. Second favorite is the Aesir (gotta love smacking giants around), third favorite the Tuatha de Danaan (hey Cu Chulainn, what's a warp spasm OH GOD).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T08:04:36-07:00","id":991856,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm not exactly new to Scion, or the community, but here goes.<br /> <br /> Hello everyone!<br /> My name is Spencer. I'm 23, and a white guy. <br /> My experiences in Tabletop include GURPS, DND, Pathfinder, and a failed DM attempt in SCION and Fragged Empire.<br /> Scion was the first game that really caught my eye, and I collected the 1E physical books. I have a vested interest in the Tuatha and Theoi, mostly as my wealth of knowledge is in those two, though I need to learn more about the Tuatha.<br /> I am going to begin trying to learn more about the Gallic, Welsh, and other pantheons that catch my eye, along with the Irish one.<br /> I'm a huge gaming, entertainment, and general geeky nerd. So im down for geek out sessions whenever!<br /> Current favorite pantheons are the Tuatha, Theoi, and Aesir, but im really excited for the others coming. I am learning and attempting to follow the Theoi and Tuatha as they're the ones that I resonate with. I'm learning. <br /> <br /> This game sits near my heart, and I love that we such a strong and vibrant community. Its a pleasure to meet everyone, and I hope we get to be an even more awesome community.<br /> <br /> Have a good day everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8023,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","user":"Grimangel53","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:48:06-07:00","id":991904,"title":"","content":"Hey there.<br /> Another (neo)pagan popping in.<br /> Mostly drawn to Norse, Hellenic and Indian divinities in RL, and, not coincidentally, that's what's keeping me hooked on this game since 1e. But love the Tuatha, Teotl and the kami of Japan as well. Diversity is excellent.<br /> *Forever salty about Sumerian gods.jpg*<br /> Just wanted to say you guys rock. Here's to hoping every member of this community gets, while not exactly what they were expecting, at least something that will excite and inspire them with the new edition.<br /> And let's make the wait for Scion2 fun!<br /> Regards, Xan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 10-23-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:31:18-07:00","id":991949,"title":"","content":"Hello new folks.<br /> <br /> I am Watcher, I have been playing Scion for seven years or something silly now. I am a history student, wrapping my final year, and getting ready to do my Masters Degree in Celtic Studies, focusing in the Medieval Irish Mythic texts. I have done a lot of work on Houserules for first edition, updating the Pantheons to make them more accurate, and both adding and rewriting Purviews. <br /> <br /> As one could guess, my favorite Pantheon is the Tuatha. If anyone wants reading suggestions for them, just send me a message, and I can hook you up with more accessible versions of Mythic texts that are in public domain and thereby up online in various places for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:19:41-07:00","id":992009,"title":"","content":"Hey all I'm Corax. Not exactly new but I have an excuse to introduce myself, I've been following Scion's 2nd edition since it was first announced and am overjoyed the game is getting so much love now.<br /> <br /> I'm a 24 year old humanities major from Baton Rouge, Louisiana and president of my college's mythology club. I've also been GMing games with them for two years now and it's been a real joy to introduce new people to the hobby, needless to say they're very keen on checking out Scion once our current campaign finishes up.<br /> <br /> Mythology wise my favorite pantheons are the Orisha and the Aesir, and my favorite myths usually revolve around trickster gods and vengeful goddesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:28:46-07:00","id":992013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=992009#post992009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all I'm Corax. Not exactly new but I have an excuse to introduce myself, I've been following Scion's 2nd edition since it was first announced and am overjoyed the game is getting so much love now.<br /> <br /> I'm a 24 year old humanities major from Baton Rouge, Louisiana and president of my college's mythology club. I've also been GMing games with them for two years now and it's been a real joy to introduce new people to the hobby, needless to say they're very keen on checking out Scion once our current campaign finishes up.<br /> <br /> Mythology wise my favorite pantheons are the Orisha and the Aesir, and my favorite myths usually revolve around trickster gods and vengeful goddesses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's nice to have you on board! I'd be super excited if my college had a Mythology club, especially one that could meet up for a good game of Scion. It's also nice to see some Orisha love, they don't get half as much attention as they deserve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:18:59-07:00","id":992053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimangel53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991856#post991856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm not exactly new to Scion, or the community, but here goes.<br /> <br /> Hello everyone!<br /> My name is Spencer. I'm 23, and a white guy.<br /> My experiences in Tabletop include GURPS, DND, Pathfinder, and a failed DM attempt in SCION and Fragged Empire.<br /> Scion was the first game that really caught my eye, and I collected the 1E physical books. I have a vested interest in the Tuatha and Theoi, mostly as my wealth of knowledge is in those two, though I need to learn more about the Tuatha.<br /> I am going to begin trying to learn more about the Gallic, Welsh, and other pantheons that catch my eye, along with the Irish one.<br /> I'm a huge gaming, entertainment, and general geeky nerd. So im down for geek out sessions whenever!<br /> Current favorite pantheons are the Tuatha, Theoi, and Aesir, but im really excited for the others coming. I am learning and attempting to follow the Theoi and Tuatha as they're the ones that I resonate with. I'm learning.<br /> <br /> This game sits near my heart, and I love that we such a strong and vibrant community. Its a pleasure to meet everyone, and I hope we get to be an even more awesome community.<br /> <br /> Have a good day everyone!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh goodness, another GURPS player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:29:02-07:00","id":992060,"title":"","content":"I'm Belle Sorciere on kickstarter.<br /> <br /> I've been playing RPGs since 1980 when I came across a game of Traveller. After that it was a matter of getting into D&amp;D, Champions, Call of Cthulhu, Runequest, and others. In the late 90s it was Shadowrun and GURPS. In the early 90s it was Vampire: The Masquerade, followed by Werewolf, Mage, Wraith, and Changeling. In the late 90s it was Trinity and Aberrant. In the early 2000s it was D&amp;D 3e and Exalted. I went through a long hiatus after I bought into the new WoD in 2004 - mostly due to not having any outlet to play, not because I didn't like the nWoD. I came back to tabletop gaming over the past few years when friends started gifting me with things like backing Mage 20 and Exalted 3e. During the hiatus I kept up my purchasing of Exalted 2e and Scion products but I never really got the chance to play them.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm planning to run a Vampire: The Requiem chronicle as soon as I move to Seattle. I have players lined up but right now we're too far away for playing to be feasible. This is fine as I am still in preparation.<br /> <br /> Scion went on kickstarter at the absolutely perfect time as I have more income to spare for kickstarters and new books than I did before. So I admit I splurged a bit on Scion, and I. Regret. Nothing. I am really looking forward to the new edition as it sounds like everything people had trouble with in 1e is being addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:28:29-07:00","id":992097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=991734#post991734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lot of us out here!<br /> <br /> I'm a staunch atheist, but I'm a anthropologist with a lifelong love of myth, so I'm in for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who's very recently come out, it's really amazing to see just how queer most roleplaying spaces are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:43:50-07:00","id":992217,"title":"","content":"I answer to Iry pretty much everywhere!<br /> <br /> I've been doing roleplaying games since 1986 when my father sat me down in front of the Commodore 64 and introduced me to Pool of Radiance. After that came 1st Edition D&amp;D I picked up in a garage sale. I spend most of my time behind the GM/Storyteller screen, but make an effort to do both to maintain perspective and not get too controlling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've been posting on these boards (and the ones that came before) since before the dawn of time. I'm one of the developers for the <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion 2.0 Fan Project</a>, and I spend a silly amount of every day researching Mythology (though Watcher has me beat). I don't have a favorite pantheon, but I want to give props to the Yoruba and Tuatha for having some of the most hilarious myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T23:22:20-07:00","id":992276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=992097#post992097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who's very recently come out, it's really amazing to see just how queer most roleplaying spaces are.</div> </div> </div> </div>A place for us to express ourselves!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T05:01:05-07:00","id":992334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=992060#post992060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Belle Sorciere on kickstarter.<br /> <br /> I've been playing RPGs since 1980 when I came across a game of Traveller. After that it was a matter of getting into D&amp;D, Champions, Call of Cthulhu, Runequest, and others. In the late 90s it was Shadowrun and GURPS. In the early 90s it was Vampire: The Masquerade, followed by Werewolf, Mage, Wraith, and Changeling. In the late 90s it was Trinity and Aberrant. In the early 2000s it was D&amp;D 3e and Exalted. I went through a long hiatus after I bought into the new WoD in 2004 - mostly due to not having any outlet to play, not because I didn't like the nWoD. I came back to tabletop gaming over the past few years when friends started gifting me with things like backing Mage 20 and Exalted 3e. During the hiatus I kept up my purchasing of Exalted 2e and Scion products but I never really got the chance to play them.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm planning to run a Vampire: The Requiem chronicle as soon as I move to Seattle. I have players lined up but right now we're too far away for playing to be feasible. This is fine as I am still in preparation.<br /> <br /> Scion went on kickstarter at the absolutely perfect time as I have more income to spare for kickstarters and new books than I did before. So I admit I splurged a bit on Scion, and I. Regret. Nothing. I am really looking forward to the new edition as it sounds like everything people had trouble with in 1e is being addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bwell,thats another GURPS Player. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5226_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5226\" data-vbnamecard=\"5226\">Jachra</a> seems like we have a few in this thread.<br /> <br /> Dont worry, i splurged too. I'm, really excited for whats coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T05:55:28-07:00","id":992342,"title":"","content":"I have quite a collection of GURPS books (both 3e and 4e), though I've never been particularly successful at actually running a game in either edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T06:31:26-07:00","id":992355,"title":"","content":"a friend of mine ran one involving dragon riders and the players either being a rider or a dragon<br /> <br /> it was a good time, and i vaporized a large hole in a massive golem and parts of a floating city. nevermind flying through a window at 60mph, forgetting my armor ring and somehow surviving, to then grab a piece of shattered glass, slice the back of a dude's neck open just enough for me to be able to reach in with my other hand and pull out an acid emitting bug and still not die from that.<br /> Gurps was fun, and im hoping I can pull something epic like that off in a SCION game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:46:53-07:00","id":992511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=992342#post992342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have quite a collection of GURPS books (both 3e and 4e), though I've never been particularly successful at actually running a game in either edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've run a number of small games in it and two large games. The first one was a sort of Viking-ish fantasy that did pretty well for a while but fell victim to player disruption.<br /> <br /> The second was a modern occult game that lasted for a bit over a year, quite successful.<br /> <br /> Oh, and a Star Wars game I've run off-and-on for like 5 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:15:11-07:00","id":992522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=992511#post992511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've run a number of small games in it and two large games. The first one was a sort of Viking-ish fantasy that did pretty well for a while but fell victim to player disruption.<br /> <br /> The second was a modern occult game that lasted for a bit over a year, quite successful.<br /> <br /> Oh, and a Star Wars game I've run off-and-on for like 5 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just never really been able to get my players to play GURPS.<br /> <br /> Tried, once, for a Space game and it just didn't work out which destroyed any chance of them trying again in the future.<br /> <br /> Oh well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do like GURPS books, in general, even if I haven't really gotten to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T15:24:56-07:00","id":992585,"title":"","content":"Im Je<span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">d, I've </span></span></span>p<span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">laye</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">d </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> r</span></span></span>pgs since I was young off an<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">d</span></span></span> on. Mostly D<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">n</span></span></span>D<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> and </span></span></span>Pathfinder, but some Sha<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">dowrun and World of </span></span></span>Darkness. I love myths, but am not very fluent in any mythology besi<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">des Greek. Also a huge fan of urban fantasy like Scion. Su</span></span></span>per excite<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">d for 2.0.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12581-jedkight","name":"jedkight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:57:11-07:00","id":992657,"title":"","content":"Anyone here planning on adding more once the backer kitt hits?<br /> <br /> I know if I can I want to add the ST screen and a few more sets of dice. Sadly just did not have the money at the time of the end for the KS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:24:55-07:00","id":992665,"title":"","content":"I'm going to get some dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:56:00-07:00","id":992713,"title":"","content":"Hello! <br /> <br /> I am spencer fox from the kickstarter. I started playing rpgs with D&amp;D 3.5 and I have since played 3.5, 4e, pathfinder, D20 modern, and Call of Cthulhu. <br /> <br /> My favorite pantheon is the Tuatha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12592-kitsune","name":"Kitsune","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:09:08-07:00","id":992773,"title":"","content":"I go by Nalak, sorry not fond of sharing my real name on forums. I actually started playing table top games at the tail end of DnD 3.5 got more into it playing 4th, (For all it's flaws it did make it so much easier to learn the ropes of the game.) When my group started branching out we had actually considered the previous edition of Scion though for one reason or another we ended up with Exalted (I regret nothing :3), Mostly we play Pathfinder in my group, but we each tend to have our own games so one of my friends runs OWoD and CWoD, another runs Deadlands,and I run Exalted and Strange. Though I cede those rarely ever happen due to one reason or another. <br /> <br /> Honestly, Scion seems more interesting this time around since it feels more like the setting has to deal with the fact that these demigods and monsters are running around and not hiding their existence as much as it felt like last edition. Though my primary interest always falls to the fact that I just like mythology and while this isn't going to be absolutely perfect on those it is still interesting to see the different pantheons and how they function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:09:38-07:00","id":992776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks#post991151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tell us a little about yourself</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YEwlW5sHQ4Q\" data-code=\"YEwlW5sHQ4Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YEwlW5sHQ4Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But I will say my favorite pantheon is the Theoi. I'm boring like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:14:12-07:00","id":993036,"title":"","content":"Right. Might as well do this. I go by many names, but almost none of which will pop up with any frequency due to my tendency to lurk rather than actively discuss. Started with horridly unbalanced homebrew in the early 2000s and moved to D&amp;D and WoD from there. The full list of systems played would both take too much effort and seem too much like a dick measuring contest for my liking. As per favored pantheon... eh. I have a few I like, but none are really favored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/991151-introductions-for-new-folks?p=992776#post992776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YEwlW5sHQ4Q\" data-code=\"YEwlW5sHQ4Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YEwlW5sHQ4Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But I will say my favorite pantheon is the Theoi. I'm boring like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You amuse me, good sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12580-iariphos","name":"Iariphos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12580_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:41:18-07:00","id":993449,"title":"","content":"Might as well get this out of the way...<br /> <br /> Hey all, I'm Crofter from Finland, commonly also known as Hero, since that's my last name. You probably won't be seeing a lot of me, I'm a lurker by nature.<br /> <br /> My favourite pantheon is probably the Teotl, although I do like the Theoi and the Aesir. Oh, and the Finnish one; pretty much due to a single myth about the gods going on a hunt for boar. The boar was more terrible than expected, and every god ended up climbing up a tree in fear. Gotta love that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12586-crofter","name":"Crofter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:21:47-07:00","id":993701,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the new faces, hi to the familiar ones, and hey all around! My name's Pedro, and i'm a 29 year old spanish guy. I answer to Phersus in these OPP fora and i've been here since their creation, coming from the old ones. <br /> <br /> Mythology has always been one of my personal hobbies thanks to my uncle, and so when i discovered Scion 5 years ago i was completely delighted. The concept was and is absolutely great, so i talked with one friend of mine about it and she quickly brought another two players, which i did not know very well. I owe Scion more than just hours of amusement for that, and thus it has a very special place in my heart; these pals i've talked about are nowadays some of my closest friends. We had these conflictive, driven characters, smashed together in some disfunctional group of shorts. We were fighting between us as much as protecting each other from outer threats, and somewhere along the road we found ourselves growing with our characters, and out of them. This is absolutely no new thing in roleplaying, but well, Scion was that game for me. <br /> <br /> So,,, yes, forgive the ramble. My three chosen Pantheons are the Theoi, the Netjer and the Tuatha, though the Teotl are always close, In the end, my favourites are the Tuatha; beacuse of the feelings and familiarity (and besides, Lugh is simply too much! xD) [By the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>, if you read this, i'd love to have some more information and myths about the Tuatha. I think i know the basics, as i've done quite a bit of research on my own, but having a proper history student pointing at quality mythology sites is simply too good to pass! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />]<br /> <br /> All the group contributed to the Kickstarter, and we are impatiently waiting for more details as we start to flesh the new chronicle.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:28:43-07:00","id":993704,"title":"","content":"I wish I could actually decide which pantheon I like best. Of those included in 2e, I really love the Theoi, Aesir, Netjer, Tuatha, Orishas, Shen, and Vedic.<br /> <br /> My first character, should I have the opportunity to play, will likely be a chosen of Brigid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}